

function plumed_preliminary_test(){
# check if the README contains the word GROMACS and if gromacs has been already configured
  grep -q GROMACS README 1>/dev/null 2>/dev/null
}

function plumed_patch_info(){
cat << EOF
A basic PLUMED interface is already present in GROMACS

This patch provides extra features to be implemented in the official PLUMED integration in the next GROMACS version, including:

- multiple walkers (GREX)
- OpenMP thread count passed to PLUMED
- ENERGY CV and energy biasing (OPES multithermal, well-tempered ensemble):
  the native GROMACS module does not compute or pass the potential energy
- checkpoints: PLUMED is told before the force calculation that GROMACS writes a checkpoint,
  so that it writes its own checkpoint data on the same step
- stop requests (e.g. COMMITTOR): GROMACS stops one step after the next step at which it communicates signals,
  writing a checkpoint
- polarizable models with shells: PLUMED updates once per step (with ENERGY, before the shells
  are relaxed: mdrun warns about it)

This patch targets the development version of GROMACS (2027.0, the main branch), which
changes often: it may not apply to, or compile with, a newer checkout of it.

Patching must be done in the gromacs root directory  _before_ the cmake command is invoked.

The GROMACS integration has some improvements with the compatibility with the multi-threading implementation
but it is still preferable to configure gromacs as

cmake -DGMX_THREAD_MPI=OFF and add -DGMX_MPI=ON if you want to use MPI.

To enable PLUMED in a gromacs simulation one should use
mdrun with an extra -plumed flag. The flag can be used to
specify the name of the PLUMED input file, e.g.:

gmx mdrun -plumed plumed.dat

For more information on gromacs you should visit http://www.gromacs.org

EOF
}

plumed_before_patch(){
  plumed_patch_info
}

PLUMED_PATCH_NO_INCLUDE=true

#this will be added later
#PLUMED_PATCH_EXTRA_FILES="src/external/plumed/PlumedInclude.h src/external/plumed/PlumedKernel.cpp src/gromacs/applied_forces/plumed/PlumedOutside.cpp src/gromacs/applied_forces/plumed/PlumedOutside.h"
